{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7HbppkdoALgKaqcPLAT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<final_document>\nSubject: Request for Promotion to Senior Paralegal\n\nDear [Managing Partner's name],\n\nI'm writing to ask to be promoted to Senior Paralegal in the litigation group. I've been a paralegal here for five years. I believe my work over that time, and especially in the past year, shows I'm ready for the role.\n\n**Workload and results.** I support four lawyers. Last year I worked on 23 cases, two of which went to trial. I billed 1,640 hours, which is 90 hours above the group's target of 1,550.\n\n**Systems others rely on.** In 2023 I built the group's tracking sheet for court deadlines. Two other groups in the firm now use it as well.\n\nThat sheet also reflects a lesson I took seriously. Last March I entered a filing deadline wrong. Another paralegal caught the error, and we filed two hours before the court's cutoff. The mistake was mine, and I fixed the process: I added a second-person check to the sheet so that a deadline no longer depends on one person's entry. That safeguard is now built into the tool.\n\n**Training and supervision.** A senior paralegal supervises the other paralegals, and I'm already doing much of that work. I trained all three paralegals the group hired in the last two years. I'd welcome formal responsibility for their development and for how the group's paralegal work is organized.\n\nI'd appreciate the chance to discuss this with you, including the pay that comes with the position. Thank you for considering my request.\n\nSincerely,\n[Your name]\n</final_document>\n\nThe letter is about 270 words, so you have room to add a specific example, such as your role in one of the trials.\n\n**About the March error:** I included it on purpose. The managing partner probably already knows about it, and raising it yourself along with the fix shows judgment, which matters for a supervisory role. If you'd rather leave it out, you can cut that paragraph and the letter still works.\n\n**About the pay:** I mentioned it without naming the $9,000 figure. If you'd rather state it, change the closing to \"including the $9,000 salary adjustment that comes with the position.\""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5391,"cache_read_input_tokens":3853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5391},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dcacb948-ec2d-4baf-80f1-6cf07e32490b","uuid":"24925abe-baa9-47e6-8ec7-3922fb80dc7c","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:05:50.407Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7HbpcLkr6BQryMic2Ub"}
